# HTTP Response Cache

When adding or changing HTTP resources, wire the shared Redis response cache. Do not ship read endpoints without a cache namespace, or mutations without invalidation.

## Decorators

- `@CacheRoute({ namespace: '<resource>' })` on **GET** handlers that return resource data (list, detail, options, `me` reads).
- `@InvalidateCache('<resource>')` on **POST / PATCH / PUT / DELETE** (and any other mutation) that changes data under that namespace.

Implementations live in:

- [`src/common/cache/decorators/cache-route.decorator.ts`](src/common/cache/decorators/cache-route.decorator.ts)
- [`src/common/cache/decorators/invalidate-cache.decorator.ts`](src/common/cache/decorators/invalidate-cache.decorator.ts)

Keys already include path, query, lang, and authenticated `userId` when present — user-scoped reads (e.g. `/merchant/me`) stay isolated.

## Namespace rules

- One stable kebab-case namespace per resource family (examples: `merchant-types`, `merchants`).
- Reuse the **same** namespace string for every `@CacheRoute` and `@InvalidateCache` of that family.
- Prefer a module-local constant (`const USERS_CACHE_NS = 'users'`).

## When to apply

| Handler | Required |
|---|---|
| GET list / detail / options / me (resource reads) | `@CacheRoute` |
| POST / PATCH / PUT / DELETE that mutates that resource | `@InvalidateCache` |
| Auth login/register, health, pure actions with no cached reads | omit (unless a related cached view must refresh) |

## Invalidation

- Any successful mutation must invalidate the namespace so lists, details, options, and `me` caches refresh.
- Direct DB writes in seeds/tests bypass decorators — call `CacheService.bumpNamespace('<resource>')` when those tests assert cached GET freshness (see merchant-types e2e).

## Anti-patterns

- Caching GETs but forgetting `@InvalidateCache` on create/update/delete
- Different namespace strings for the same resource on read vs write
- Caching endpoints that must always be real-time without a clear product reason (document if intentionally uncached)
- Relying on TTL alone instead of invalidation after writes

## Checklist for new endpoints

1. Choose / reuse the resource cache namespace.
2. Add `@CacheRoute` on GETs that serve that resource.
3. Add `@InvalidateCache` on every mutation of that resource.
4. Cover list/detail freshness in e2e when cache matters.
